WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:02.340
<i>We scored.</i>

00:02.540 --> 00:05.840
<i>We finally scored in the fourth stage
of the Grand Finals.</i>

00:06.340 --> 00:08.630
<i>Don Wei almost found out
who I was.</i>

00:08.800 --> 00:10.680
<i>But he's still not ready
to be a father.</i>

00:10.890 --> 00:11.800
Listen here.

00:11.970 --> 00:14.600
Have you ever heard of
the Stern Boarding School, young lady?

00:15.680 --> 00:17.140
I'll be more direct.

00:18.270 --> 00:21.150
Are you my daughter, Eva?

00:22.110 --> 00:24.940
If I were your daughter,
you would know it immediately.

00:25.110 --> 00:27.360
I mean, you really wouldn't need
to ask me, would you?

00:28.820 --> 00:30.950
Oh, Eva, it's you.

01:59.200 --> 02:00.080
Morning, sir.

02:00.540 --> 02:01.250
Up here.

02:19.310 --> 02:20.930
A penny for your thoughts?

02:27.190 --> 02:28.650
Maya?

02:32.440 --> 02:35.450
I hope you haven't forgotten
our special date.

02:35.660 --> 02:37.530
Tonight's our anniversary.

02:38.240 --> 02:39.620
How could I forget that?

02:59.930 --> 03:00.890
Thank you.

03:06.980 --> 03:10.150
You've really pulled out all the stops
tonight, haven't you?

03:10.320 --> 03:11.730
I don't know what you mean.

03:18.280 --> 03:20.530
May I have the pleasure,
Madame Wei?

03:21.910 --> 03:24.120
You married a racer,
not a dancer.

03:24.500 --> 03:26.830
But if you want
to take the risk.

03:28.960 --> 03:31.290
I've never actually
waltzed before.

03:31.750 --> 03:33.710
Just follow me, princess.

03:48.350 --> 03:50.230
Oops. I told you.

03:50.770 --> 03:52.230
You're doing just fine.

04:17.010 --> 04:19.430
I wish every night
could be like this.

04:19.590 --> 04:21.510
Be careful what you wish for.

04:22.640 --> 04:24.430
You might just get it.

04:32.770 --> 04:34.110
Mommy, Daddy!

04:34.320 --> 04:37.030
Who look who's here.
It's my little champion.

04:38.860 --> 04:40.610
She's really alive tonight.

04:41.620 --> 04:43.160
Shouldn't you be in bed?

04:43.330 --> 04:45.040
How could you abandon me?

04:45.200 --> 04:46.950
My poor baby.

04:47.250 --> 04:49.210
It's OK now. We're back.

04:57.630 --> 05:01.010
You've made me
the happiest man in the world.

05:38.090 --> 05:40.130
Come on, Jordan.
Up, up, up!

05:40.300 --> 05:42.300
We're in competition, remember?

05:43.930 --> 05:45.010
What's up with her?

06:06.740 --> 06:08.200
Feeling better?

06:09.410 --> 06:12.080
What do you mean, better?
I'm feeling super great.

06:12.410 --> 06:13.710
We're fourth in the rankings.

06:13.870 --> 06:16.080
That's only three points
behind the leaders.

06:19.920 --> 06:21.590
That's why we're here.

06:26.340 --> 06:28.760
Who cares if my father
is a complete disaster

06:28.970 --> 06:30.720
and my best friend
just betrayed me?

06:31.060 --> 06:32.770
All I have is the race.

06:32.930 --> 06:34.520
And that's all I need.

06:35.650 --> 06:39.150
Hey, this isn't still
about Don Wei, is it?

06:39.520 --> 06:43.450
Because if it is,
it's a real waste of time.

06:47.320 --> 06:49.240
Molly, just stand up
in front of him and say,

06:49.530 --> 06:50.830
"you're a loser!"

06:51.240 --> 06:52.370
Sir!

06:52.790 --> 06:54.210
Good morning.

06:54.540 --> 06:56.170
Good morning, Jordan.

06:57.130 --> 06:58.790
Where is your partner?

06:58.960 --> 07:01.050
I have something important
to tell her.

07:01.210 --> 07:02.210
I don't know.

07:02.340 --> 07:04.630
But she must be
around here somewhere.

07:10.350 --> 07:12.890
Space would be
a terrible place for me to die.

07:18.940 --> 07:20.360
Rivers and deep canyons.

07:20.690 --> 07:22.110
We can handle that.

07:23.650 --> 07:26.030
-Molly, I...
-I wouldn't be so sure.

07:26.450 --> 07:28.990
That yellow stone is made
of high density sulfur,

07:29.200 --> 07:31.450
extremely flammable stuff.

07:32.620 --> 07:35.660
Wow, those rivers
are pure acid.

07:35.870 --> 07:37.370
That's not possible.

07:38.080 --> 07:39.920
What's not possible?

07:41.130 --> 07:42.960
If the Whizzing Arrow 3
takes a dip,

07:43.130 --> 07:45.920
its hull will disintegrate
in three seconds.

07:49.010 --> 07:50.260
That's not good.

07:50.430 --> 07:53.310
Whatever. The other racers
face the same risk.

07:54.020 --> 07:56.180
-Let's go.
-Molly, wait.

07:56.600 --> 07:58.400
<i>-Yes?
-I...</i>

07:58.560 --> 08:00.650
I don't want you to race today.

08:00.860 --> 08:01.520
What?

08:02.020 --> 08:03.610
It's too dangerous.

08:03.820 --> 08:05.440
We'll just have to sit this one out.

08:05.860 --> 08:08.410
We'll concentrate all of our efforts
on the next race.

08:08.570 --> 08:11.120
Could there really be
a beating heart in that body?

08:11.280 --> 08:12.700
No, not a chance.

08:12.910 --> 08:14.700
This is definitely
some kind of trick.

08:15.040 --> 08:16.120
We don't have a choice.

08:16.290 --> 08:18.870
There are only five races left.
You know that.

08:19.080 --> 08:21.290
Unless you still don't
trust me as a pilot.

08:21.500 --> 08:23.040
Molly, listen here.

08:23.290 --> 08:27.260
I... I just don't want you
to get hurt. You understand?

08:28.010 --> 08:30.390
I couldn't forgive myself if you did.

08:38.230 --> 08:41.060
I'm sorry.
It's go time. And I'm the pilot.

08:41.560 --> 08:43.730
I won that privilege
the hard way.

08:44.190 --> 08:45.730
I'll decide for myself.

08:46.570 --> 08:47.940
Uh, Molly!

08:48.650 --> 08:51.360
I'm telling you, you got him
all wrong. He's not a robot.

08:52.780 --> 08:55.040
Come on!
The race is about to start.

08:56.080 --> 08:58.080
Jordan, stay where you are.

08:58.460 --> 08:59.830
We're going to sit out this race.

09:00.330 --> 09:01.750
Sit out the race?

09:01.920 --> 09:04.670
Jordan, hurry.
There's no time to lose.

09:06.460 --> 09:07.130
Sorry.

09:07.630 --> 09:08.800
<i>|</i> gotta go-

09:13.050 --> 09:15.510
I guess stubbornness
runs in the family.

09:17.060 --> 09:17.810
Yes, sir?

09:19.060 --> 09:20.940
You heard them.
Make sure everything's set.

09:52.550 --> 09:55.680
100 meters. <i>75</i> meters. 50.
She's falling too fast!

09:59.930 --> 10:00.730
OK, now!

10:08.780 --> 10:10.740
Keep it up, Molly.
You're fifth.

10:12.110 --> 10:13.660
And the first gate is just ahead.

10:25.040 --> 10:26.710
Good try, Muir.

10:26.880 --> 10:29.920
But I'm afraid you're about
to plunge in the ranking.

10:43.690 --> 10:44.600
I see the gate.

10:51.530 --> 10:52.610
What happened to that thing!

11:26.770 --> 11:28.440
Hang on, Eva. You can do it.

11:30.570 --> 11:31.900
Molly, you can do it.

11:40.580 --> 11:41.870
What did we ever do to him?

11:59.010 --> 12:02.350
Let us go.
I have to win this race!

12:14.280 --> 12:15.780
Molly. get out!

12:15.940 --> 12:16.900
Get out!

12:20.240 --> 12:23.910
Stan, Koji,
override the trapdoor lock, now!

12:24.410 --> 12:25.080
Almost there.

12:32.420 --> 12:34.500
No, no, leave me alone!

13:09.790 --> 13:14.090
Molly! No!

13:20.470 --> 13:21.720
Automatic pilot switched on.

13:21.970 --> 13:23.220
I've got the steering.

13:23.430 --> 13:24.850
-You take the reactors.
-Got it.

13:46.530 --> 13:48.040
Where am I?

14:28.700 --> 14:30.910
Why have you brought me here?

14:33.500 --> 14:36.290
I'm not sure,
but I feel you won't hurt me.

14:42.840 --> 14:45.130
Is this what you wanted to show me?

14:52.850 --> 14:55.020
I... I don't understand you.

16:31.990 --> 16:35.580
These telepathic tentacles
will make us a fortune.

16:35.830 --> 16:38.460
Just remove them quick,
so we can get out of here.

17:28.590 --> 17:32.640
You want the Ultimate Prize
so you can bring her back.

17:33.970 --> 17:35.180
That's right, isn't it?

17:50.700 --> 17:53.070
Just the way
I hope to bring back...

17:54.240 --> 17:55.950
...my mother.

18:06.540 --> 18:09.050
Don't worry, Jordan.
We're bringing you in.

18:10.260 --> 18:12.090
What's the use now?

18:27.150 --> 18:28.440
Molly!

18:29.190 --> 18:32.070
Sir, look, it's her.

18:36.280 --> 18:38.330
It's truly a miracle.

18:46.580 --> 18:47.420
Molly?

18:48.210 --> 18:49.920
Molly, can you hear me?

18:52.550 --> 18:54.220
Hello there, Jordan.

18:55.090 --> 18:57.050
A penny for your thoughts?

19:45.690 --> 19:48.690
Don Wei!
What a pleasant surprise.

19:49.060 --> 19:51.110
With all we've been facing
here on Earth,

19:51.270 --> 19:53.360
I didn't even have a chance
to congratulate you

19:53.570 --> 19:54.820
on your first victory.

19:55.740 --> 19:56.950
Mr. President,

19:57.110 --> 19:59.950
you asked me to carry the team
as far as I could.

20:00.450 --> 20:02.030
We made it
through the preselections,

20:02.200 --> 20:04.700
and even scored
one victory on Oban.

20:05.540 --> 20:08.330
But this is as far
as the team goes.

20:08.620 --> 20:09.960
We're pulling out.

20:10.420 --> 20:13.710
Have you gone mad?
We cannot stop halfway.

20:13.880 --> 20:16.090
Have you forgotten
what's at stake here?

20:16.300 --> 20:17.300
Mr. President,

20:17.470 --> 20:19.970
we almost lost
our second pilot today...

20:20.510 --> 20:21.470
a teenager,

20:21.640 --> 20:24.430
years too young
for this level of danger.

20:25.890 --> 20:28.020
She also happens
to be my daugh-

20:28.190 --> 20:30.560
Don Wei, we are not
going to quit now.

20:30.730 --> 20:31.940
Do you hear me?

20:32.360 --> 20:33.860
My choice is final.

20:34.020 --> 20:36.280
That choice is not yours to make.

20:36.440 --> 20:37.900
We have just
received information

20:38.070 --> 20:40.570
that the Crogs have started
to gather their troops

20:40.740 --> 20:41.740
on our very borders.

20:41.910 --> 20:43.160
They will annihilate us

20:43.330 --> 20:45.790
as soon as the truce
of the Great Race is lifted.

20:46.290 --> 20:49.000
I'm afraid there's nothing
I can do about that.

20:49.170 --> 20:51.330
If the Crogs win
the Ultimate Prize,

20:51.580 --> 20:55.090
they'll wipe every single
one of us into oblivion.

20:55.300 --> 20:57.340
Only you and your team
can stop them.

20:57.670 --> 20:59.130
But sir, I...

20:59.300 --> 21:02.220
Whether you like it or not,
our future,

21:02.390 --> 21:04.510
the future
of the entire human race,

21:04.680 --> 21:06.970
lies squarely
on your shoulders, Don Wei.

21:20.400 --> 21:23.530
Must I pay
with my own daughter?
